{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1699 (commit 032d648ebe, rebased onto origin/main 61b49deaa6).\n\nWHAT LANDED IN THE CHANGE (12 files):\n* _config_schema.py — both resolved_statuses fields + their two _as_str_list coercer entries deleted. _as_str_list KEPT: it still has scan_roots / include_extensions callers, so the plan's conditional 'delete the helper if this was its last caller' resolves to keep. Module drops 798 -> 784 lines against the 800 cap, so the module-size gate got easier rather than harder.\n* _deprecations.py — the two 549c _scheduled rows dropped; four warn-class tombstones added (cfg jira.resolved_statuses, cfg reconciler.resolved_statuses, and the auto-derived env twins REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES / REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES); historical NOTE appended recording the operator-approved 2026-08-12 removal alongside the sibling 97d4 / 6cc4 notes.\n* Tests — test_config_resolved_statuses_deprecation.py replaced by test_config_resolved_statuses_removal.py (15 tests, mirroring the 6cc4 deprecation->removal rename). Heldout config-read pin flips from exactly-two parked markers to exactly-zero.\n* Docs — key removed from docs/config.md and docs/user-guide.md; release-notes.md + CHANGELOG.md entries added.\n* Two DC adapter docstrings that pointed at the now-deleted JiraConfig.resolved_statuses were retargeted at the tombstone registry.\n\nTOMBSTONE CLASS — warn, not error. Recorded because it is the one judgement call in this change. _deprecations.py codifies error for an operationally load-bearing removed input and warn for an inert one. These keys are inert: nothing read them and the behaviour they configured no longer exists, so a still-set key must not abort the command. This deliberately does NOT copy sibling ticket 6cc4's error choice for REBAR_LLM_MODEL, whose stated rationale — silently ignoring a set model id would quietly change which model every operation runs — is exactly the load-bearing argument that does not transfer to an inert key. It follows the inert-cfg precedent instead (code_health.enabled, code_health.analyzers, reconciler.lock_backend, reconciler.lock_max_retries), which is also what this ticket's own acceptance criteria specify.\n\nVERIFIED BEHAVIOUR (end-to-end, not just unit): a config still setting BOTH keys loads successfully, sibling keys in the same sections survive, each removed key is dropped with 'was removed in v1.0.0 (no replacement; it is now ignored)' on the rebar logger, and the env twins warn without raising.\n\nLOCAL GATES: all ten check_* gates green; the four generators produce no diff; make lint and make typecheck (515 files) green. The config-read gate explicitly reports 'all dataclass fields are read' — no orphaned # read-via: markers. Full pytest re-run on the rebased tree is in flight; awaiting Verified +1 before close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786590015803714001,"uuid":"1435c54a-30c5-4b06-8768-e3e5475c3c83"}